Service_Stubby_Title=DNS-over-TLS (Stubby)
Service_Stubby_Desc=Stubby sends DNS queries through authenticated DNS-over-TLS. In router DNS mode, dnsmasq does not fall back to ordinary provider DNS, so keep Stubby disabled until at least one working resolver is configured.
Service_Stubby_DNSList_Help=Add up to four DNS-over-TLS resolvers.
Service_Stubby_Enable=Enable Stubby?
Service_Stubby_Mode=Operating mode
Service_Stubby_Mode_Desc=Strict mode uses authenticated TLS only. Opportunistic mode may also use unencrypted DNS. Standalone listens separately; router DNS mode sends dnsmasq queries to Stubby.
Service_Stubby_Mode_Menu0=Strict, standalone
Service_Stubby_Mode_Menu1=Strict, router DNS
Service_Stubby_Mode_Menu2=Opportunistic, standalone
Service_Stubby_Mode_Menu3=Opportunistic, router DNS
Service_Stubby_RoundRobin=Round-robin queries
Service_Stubby_Resolvers_Header=DNS resolvers
Service_Stubby_Alert_Empty=No DNS-over-TLS resolver is configured. Add one before enabling Stubby.
Service_Stubby_Alert_Invalid=Enter a valid resolver hostname and IP address. A maximum of four resolvers is supported.
Service_Stubby_Listen_Address=Listen address
Service_Stubby_Listen_Port=Listen port
Service_Stubby_Resolver_IP=Resolver IP address
Service_Stubby_Resolver_Name=Resolver authentication name
Service_Stubby_Loopback=loopback
Service_Stubby_All_Addresses=All IPv4 addresses
Service_Stubby_Catalog_Unavailable=Resolver list could not be loaded. You can still enter a resolver name and IP address manually.
